.TH REPORTOOLS 1 "2026-11-10" "reportools 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reportools, rt \- initialize and manage report projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reportools
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B reportools
.B \-\-help
|
.B \-\-version
|
.B \-\-env
.I shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reportools
manages reports, each kept as its own git repository.
The details of a report are stored in the project's metafile,
.IR .reportools ,
and the location of each project is stored in a path list on this machine.
Repositories are created and cloned with
.BR gh (1)
and synchronized with
.BR git (1).
.PP
.B rt
is short for
.B reportools
and becomes available once the output of
.B \-\-env
is evaluated by the shell.
.PP
Where a subcommand accepts an optional
.IR short ,
omitting it selects the project that contains the current directory.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-\fIcolumn\fR ...]
Show every report, soonest deadline first.
With columns, print only those columns, tab-separated and without a header.
.TP
.BR at " [\fIshort\fR] [" \-\-\fIcolumn\fR ...]
Show every field of a report.
With columns, print only their values, one per line.
.TP
.BI get " short"
Clone
.IR user / short
into
.RI ./ short
and add it to the path list.
.TP
.BR sync " [\fIshort\fR]"
Run
.B git pull
and then
.BR "git push" .
Nothing is committed.
With
.BR \-\-all ,
synchronize every report.
.TP
.BI init " short"
Create a project in
.RI ./ short ,
commit it and add it to the path list, then create the private repository
.IR user / short
and push.
If
.B release.title
is not set,
.B init
fails before creating anything.
.TP
.BR add " [\fIpath\fR]"
Add an existing directory to the path list.
If it has no
.IR .reportools ,
one is created from the options; without
.BR \-\-short ,
the directory name becomes the short.
.TP
.BR remove " [\fIshort\fR]"
Drop a report from the path list.
Its directory and remote repository are kept.
.TP
.BR modify " [\fIshort\fR] " \-\-\fIcolumn\fR " \fIvalue\fR ..."
Update fields of a report.
This rewrites
.I .reportools
without committing.
The short cannot be changed.
.B \-\-path
updates only the path list, and requires a
.I .reportools
in the new directory.
.TP
.BR ok " [\fIshort\fR]"
Mark a report as finished.
Same as
.B modify
.RI [ short ]
.BR "\-\-state ok" .
.TP
.B export
Print every field of every report as TSV with a header line.
.TP
.BR config " \fIkey\fR [\fIvalue\fR]"
Print or change a setting.
With
.BR \-\-list ,
print every setting that is set.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
After a subcommand, show the usage of that subcommand.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " shell"
Print shell setup for
.BR eval .
.I shell
is
.B zsh
or
.BR bash .
For
.B zsh
this is the
.B rt
alias and completion; for
.B bash
it is the alias only.
.SS Columns
These select columns for
.B list
and
.BR at ,
and take values for
.BR init ,
.B add
and
.BR modify .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-short
Identifier of the report, also used as the repository name.
Letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.B \-
only.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-title ", " \-\-long
Title of the report.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-subj ", " \-\-subject
Subject (course) name.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-in ", " \-\-deadline
Deadline, written as
.BR "YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM" .
The time of day is required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-state
One of
.BR draft ,
.BR submit ,
.B resub
or
.BR ok .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path
Directory of the project.
.TP
.B \-\-style
Project style:
.B typst
or
.BR latex .
.SS Other
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
.RB ( sync )
Act on every report.
.TP
.B \-\-list
.RB ( config )
Print every setting that is set.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B release.title
File name of the released PDF, without the extension.
Required by
.BR init .
.TP
.B init.style
Default style for
.BR init .
Defaults to
.BR typst .
.TP
.B github.user
Owner of the repositories.
Defaults to the account
.B gh
is logged in to.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/reportools/config.ini
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/reportools/reports.tsv
The path list: one line per report, holding the short and the absolute path separated by a tab.
.TP
.I .reportools
Metafile of each project, tracked by git.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
First-time setup:
.PP
.nf
.RS
reportools config release.title 12345_name
echo \(aqeval "$(reportools \-\-env zsh)"\(aq >> ~/.zshrc
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create a report and follow it until it is accepted:
.PP
.nf
.RS
rt init algo1 \-j Algorithms \-d "2026\-11\-30 23:59"
cd algo1
rt modify \-\-state submit
rt modify \-\-state resub
rt modify \-\-state submit
rt ok
.RE
.fi
.PP
Continue on another machine:
.PP
.nf
.RS
rt get algo1
rt sync algo1
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR gh (1),
.BR typst (1)
